{"type":"system","subtype":"background_tasks_changed","tasks":[{"task_id":"b14gdj6vr","task_type":"local_bash","description":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_4_repair_1; cd $D\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='candidate.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''symmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch, plus a personal\nlapse rate. The one change: the personal sensitivity no longer applies to the\nswitching-rate penalty alone; alternation sensitivity is shared and each person\nhas an overall decisiveness that scales the whole difference between the two\nimpressions, so people differ in how consistently they follow the common\nimpression (the critique's excess spread in majority agreement).''','''symmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch. The one change is\nwhere people's consistency comes from: alternation sensitivity and the guessing\nrate are shared, and each person instead has an overall decisiveness that\nscales the whole difference between the two impressions, so people differ in\nhow consistently they follow the common impression (the critique's excess\nspread in majority agreement) through decisiveness, not through personal\nguessing or a personal sensitivity to switching alone.''')\ns=s.replace('sigma_dec = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_dec\", sigma=0.7)','sigma_dec = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_dec\", sigma=0.5)')\ns=s.replace('''    # Personal lapse (guessing) rate.\n    mu_lapse = pm.Normal(\"mu_lapse\", mu=-2.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_lapse = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_lapse\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_lapse = pm.Normal(\"z_lapse\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    lapse = pm.Deterministic(\"lapse\", pm.math.sigmoid(mu_lapse + sigma_lapse * z_lapse))\n''','''    # Shared lapse (guessing) rate: personal consistency lives in decisiveness.\n    lapse = pm.Beta(\"lapse\", alpha=2.0, beta=10.0)\n''')\ns=s.replace('lam = lapse[participant_id]','lam = lapse')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > hypothesis.md <<'EOF'\nRefinement of the incumbent `complement_symmetry_aversion`: each sequence's apparent randomness is still judged by its switching rate against a personal ideal (lenient toward over-alternation), personal weights on heads/tails imbalance and the longest streak, and shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry, complement symmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch. The one change is where people's consistency comes from: instead of a personal sensitivity to the switching rate alone and a personal guessing rate, each person has their own overall decisiveness (drawn from a population) that sharpens or flattens the whole comparison of the two impressions, with one shared guessing rate — so some people follow every cue almost deterministically while others follow all of them weakly, addressing the critique (surviving FDR) that people differ in how often they agree with the majority choice more than the incumbent produces.\nEOF\ngrep -n \"lapse\\|sigma_dec\" candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && timeout 1500 /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses $D/../../responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"}],"uuid":"1bbfdbe4-130e-4397-b853-876e0aeda475","session_id":"1f45b264-65a7-4cef-ba51-b1369f7eb2b2"}
